        <!-- DAY 1 SLIDES -->
        <!-- Slide 3: Day 1 - Learning Goals -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 1: Finding Employment Help - Learning Goals</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>What Students Will Learn</h2>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Understand different types of employment support available</li>
                        <li>Learn when and how to ask for help appropriately</li>
                        <li>Identify personal strengths and support needs</li>
                        <li>Recognize that asking for help is a sign of wisdom, not weakness</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h2>Key Concepts to Teach</h2>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Support People and Their Roles:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Job Coaches:</strong> Help you learn job skills and succeed at work</li>
                        <li><strong>Employment Counselors:</strong> Help you find jobs and prepare for interviews</li>
                        <li><strong>Skills Trainers:</strong> Teach you new skills for work</li>
                        <li><strong>Transportation Services:</strong> Help you get to work</li>
                        <li><strong>Benefits Counselors:</strong> Help with understanding work and benefits</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Today's Focus: Everyone needs help sometimes - successful people know how to find and use support!
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 4: Day 1 - Teaching Strategies -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 1: Teaching Strategies</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>How to Make Employment Support Real</h2>
                
                <h3>🎯 Mini-Lesson Approach (15 minutes)</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Start with Personal Connections:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Opening Question:</strong> "When you learned to drive, who helped you? That's like a job coach!"</li>
                        <li><strong>Visual Supports:</strong> Show pictures of different support people at work</li>
                        <li><strong>Real Examples:</strong> "Who helps you learn new things right now in school?"</li>
                        <li><strong>Normalize Help-Seeking:</strong> Share how adults get help with work challenges</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📋 Worksheet Preparation</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Pre-Activity:</strong> Read each scenario aloud and discuss as a group</li>
                        <li><strong>Model One:</strong> Work through one matching example together</li>
                        <li><strong>Encourage Reflection:</strong> "Think about times you've needed help"</li>
                        <li><strong>Support During Work:</strong> Circulate to provide individual guidance</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🗣️ Discussion Prompts</h3>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    "Tell me about a time someone helped you learn something new" | "What makes asking for help hard sometimes?" | "Who are helpful people in your life?"
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 5: Day 1 - Community Connection -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 1: Community Connection</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>Connecting Students to Local Employment Support</h2>
                
                <div class="community-box">
                    <h4>Community Opportunities Employment Services</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Supported Employment:</strong> Job coaching and on-site training</li>
                        <li><strong>Job Development:</strong> Finding jobs that match student abilities</li>
                        <li><strong>Skills Assessment:</strong> Evaluating strengths and support needs</li>
                        <li><strong>Advocacy:</strong> Helping navigate workplace challenges</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🌉 Building Real Connections</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Invite Guest Speakers:</strong> Ask job coaches to visit and share their work</li>
                        <li><strong>Agency Tours:</strong> Visit local employment service offices</li>
                        <li><strong>Transition Planning:</strong> Start connecting students by age 16</li>
                        <li><strong>Family Involvement:</strong> Help families understand available services</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📞 Making First Contact</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Teacher Action Steps:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Contact Community Opportunities to discuss student needs</li>
                        <li>Schedule informational meetings for interested families</li>
                        <li>Document which students might benefit from services</li>
                        <li>Create referral timeline for graduating students</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 6: Day 1 - Assessment & Wrap-Up -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 1: Assessment & Wrap-Up</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>How to Assess Understanding</h2>
                
                <h3>✅ Quick Checks During Class</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Exit Ticket:</strong> "Name one person who can help you find a job"</li>
                        <li><strong>Thumbs Up/Down:</strong> "Is it okay to ask for help at work?"</li>
                        <li><strong>Partner Share:</strong> Students tell a partner about their strengths</li>
                        <li><strong>Reflection:</strong> "What's one thing you learned about getting help?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📊 Worksheet Assessment</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Look For:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Correct matching of situations to support people</li>
                        <li>Identification of personal strengths (any positive responses)</li>
                        <li>Recognition of support needs (realistic self-assessment)</li>
                        <li>Thoughtful reflection responses</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🔄 Preparing for Day 2</h3>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Preview: "Tomorrow we'll explore different jobs in our community. Think about what type of work interests you!"
                </div>

                <div class="goal-setting-visual" style="background: #667eea;">
                    <h3>Today's Success: Students understand that help is available and normal to seek!</h3>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- DAY 2 SLIDES -->
        <!-- Slide 7: Day 2 - Learning Goals -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 2: Jobs in My Community - Learning Goals</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>What Students Will Learn</h2>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Identify different types of jobs available locally</li>
                        <li>Understand the concept of entry-level employment</li>
                        <li>Match personal interests and skills to job types</li>
                        <li>Explore work environments and job requirements</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h2>Job Categories to Explore</h2>
                <div class="icons-grid">
                    <div class="icon-item">
                        <div class="emoji">🛍️</div>
                        <h4>Retail</h4>
                        <p>Customer service, stocking, cashier</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-item">
                        <div class="emoji">🍔</div>
                        <h4>Food Service</h4>
                        <p>Food prep, serving, cleaning</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-item">
                        <div class="emoji">🧹</div>
                        <h4>Cleaning</h4>
                        <p>Janitorial, maintenance, housekeeping</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-item">
                        <div class="emoji">📦</div>
                        <h4>Warehouse</h4>
                        <p>Sorting, packaging, organizing</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Today's Focus: There are many job options, and everyone can find work that matches their abilities!
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 8: Day 2 - Teaching Strategies -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 2: Teaching Strategies</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>Making Jobs Real and Accessible</h2>
                
                <h3>🏪 Virtual Community Tour</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Before Using the Worksheet:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Google Street View:</strong> "Visit" local businesses students know</li>
                        <li><strong>Local Connections:</strong> "Where do your family members work?"</li>
                        <li><strong>Job Spotting:</strong> Look at photos and identify different jobs</li>
                        <li><strong>Skills Inventory:</strong> "What are you good at that helps in this job?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📋 Making Matching Meaningful</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Use Real Business Names:</strong> McDonald's, Walmart, local stores students know</li>
                        <li><strong>Connect to Interests:</strong> "You like helping people - what jobs do that?"</li>
                        <li><strong>Reality Check:</strong> Discuss both good parts and challenges of jobs</li>
                        <li><strong>Progression Planning:</strong> "This could be your first job, then later..."</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🎯 Dream Job to Reality Bridge</h3>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Help students connect their interests to achievable first steps: "You want to work with animals? Let's look at pet store jobs!"
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 9: Day 2 - Community Connection -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 2: Community Connection</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>Local Job Development Opportunities</h2>
                
                <div class="community-box">
                    <h4>Community Opportunities Job Development</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Employer Partnerships:</strong> Relationships with local businesses</li>
                        <li><strong>Customized Employment:</strong> Jobs designed around student strengths</li>
                        <li><strong>Job Carving:</strong> Creating positions that match abilities</li>
                        <li><strong>Natural Supports:</strong> Training coworkers to provide ongoing help</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🏢 Building Employer Relationships</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Field Trip Planning:</strong> Visit businesses to see jobs in action</li>
                        <li><strong>Guest Speakers:</strong> Invite local employers to share about entry-level jobs</li>
                        <li><strong>Job Shadow Setup:</strong> Arrange observation opportunities</li>
                        <li><strong>Volunteer Connections:</strong> Start with unpaid experience to build skills</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📍 Local Business Mapping</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Create a Community Job Map:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Identify walking-distance employment options</li>
                        <li>Map transportation routes to major employers</li>
                        <li>Note which businesses hire entry-level workers</li>
                        <li>Track which employers work with disability services</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 10: Day 2 - Assessment & Wrap-Up -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 2: Assessment & Wrap-Up</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>Checking Job Exploration Understanding</h2>
                
                <h3>✅ Quick Assessment Activities</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Job Sort:</strong> Students categorize jobs by work environment</li>
                        <li><strong>Interest Inventory:</strong> "Point to jobs that interest you and explain why"</li>
                        <li><strong>Skills Match:</strong> "Which jobs use skills you already have?"</li>
                        <li><strong>Next Step Planning:</strong> "What would help you get ready for that job?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📊 Worksheet Assessment</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Look For:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Accurate job-to-environment matching</li>
                        <li>Realistic skill assessments for different job types</li>
                        <li>Thoughtful dream job descriptions</li>
                        <li>Connection between interests and job choices</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🔄 Preparing for Day 3</h3>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Preview: "Tomorrow we'll look at the skills you need to be successful at any job. We'll see what you're already good at!"
                </div>

                <div class="goal-setting-visual" style="background: #2196F3;">
                    <h3>Today's Success: Students can identify job options and connect them to their interests!</h3>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- DAY 3 SLIDES -->
        <!-- Slide 11: Day 3 - Learning Goals -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 3: Workplace Skills - Learning Goals</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>What Students Will Learn</h2>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Identify essential workplace skills across all job types</li>
                        <li>Complete honest self-assessment of current abilities</li>
                        <li>Set realistic goals for skill development</li>
                        <li>Understand that skills can be learned and improved</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h2>Core Workplace Skills</h2>
                <div class="resource-grid">
                    <div class="resource-card">
                        <h4>🕐 Time & Attendance</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Arriving on time consistently</li>
                            <li>Staying for complete work shifts</li>
                            <li>Taking appropriate breaks</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="resource-card">
                        <h4>💬 Communication</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Speaking politely to customers</li>
                            <li>Asking questions when needed</li>
                            <li>Working cooperatively with teams</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="resource-card">
                        <h4>⚡ Task Completion</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Following directions accurately</li>
                            <li>Staying focused on work</li>
                            <li>Working safely at all times</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="resource-card">
                        <h4>👔 Professionalism</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Dressing appropriately</li>
                            <li>Maintaining good hygiene</li>
                            <li>Showing respect to everyone</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Today's Focus: Everyone has strengths to build on and areas to improve - that's normal and positive!
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Slide 12: Day 3 - Teaching Strategies -->
        <div class="slide">
            <h1>Day 3: Teaching Strategies</h1>
            <div class="slide-content">
                <h2>Strengths-Based Skills Assessment</h2>
                
                <h3>⭐ Creating a Safe Assessment Environment</h3>
                <div class="example-box">
                    <h4>Before Self-Rating Activities:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Model Honesty:</strong> "I'm still working on being on time every day too!"</li>
                        <li><strong>Emphasize Growth:</strong> "Rating yourself a '2' means you're learning - that's great!"</li>
                        <li><strong>Real Examples:</strong> "When have you shown good teamwork at school?"</li>
                        <li><strong>Future Focus:</strong> "What skill would help you most in a job you want?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>🎯 Making Skill Development Concrete</h3>
                <div class="bullet-points">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Break It Down:</strong> "Better communication" becomes "practice saying 'good morning'"</li>
                        <li><strong>Practice Opportunities:</strong> How can they practice these skills at school/home?</li>
                        <li><strong>Support Connections:</strong> Who can help them practice each skill?</li>
                        <li><strong>Celebrate Current Strengths:</strong> Acknowledge any skill they rate as 3 or 4</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>📋 Goal Setting That Works</h3>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    Help students choose goals they can work on this week, not just distant dreams: "Practice arriving 5 minutes early to class"
